{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823442-after-a-first-reading-are-passive-kuruth-triggers-too-intense","id":823442,"title":"After a first reading - are passive Kuruth triggers too intense?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-04T09:41:42-08:00","id":823442,"title":"After a first reading - are passive Kuruth triggers too intense?","content":"I was thinking specifically of the phase of the moon one or the human blood one. In a party of 5 werewolves with 5 different auspices, who all have moon-phase Kuruth triggers and are all using the passive trigger, AT LEAST one of them goes into death rage once a night and rages all night (if the answer from the quick answer thread is correct) no matter what? Every night? Its impossible to tell any sort of story at that point, right?<br /> <br /> Or am I missing something? How did passive Kuruth triggers play out for you?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Even if one werewolf is using the moon phase passive kuruth trigger, that already seems horrible. Like, for days your group spends every night, the specific time they should be doing something, just looking after this dude and also probably going into Kuruth themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","user":"Avalon Polo","date":". 02-04-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","name":"Avalon Polo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T09:54:51-08:00","id":823452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon Polo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823442-after-a-first-reading-are-passive-kuruth-triggers-too-intense#post823442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking specifically of the phase of the moon one or the human blood one. In a party of 5 werewolves with 5 different auspices, who all have moon-phase Kuruth triggers and are all using the passive trigger, AT LEAST one of them goes into death rage once a night and rages all night (if the answer from the quick answer thread is correct) no matter what? Every night? Its impossible to tell any sort of story at that point, right?<br /> <br /> Or am I missing something? How did passive Kuruth triggers play out for you?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Even if one werewolf is using the moon phase passive kuruth trigger, that already seems horrible. Like, for days your group spends every night, the specific time they should be doing something, just looking after this dude and also probably going into Kuruth themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the price you pay for being at the extremes of Harmony. You only suffer the Passive trigger when you're at 10 or 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T09:59:21-08:00","id":823455,"title":"","content":"Oh! Hahaha, I definitely missed that part. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","name":"Avalon Polo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:46:19-08:00","id":823496,"title":"","content":"Also, it's not impossible to control. 80% of the time, the pack's Edoloth will be like &quot;stahp it&quot; and the Kuruth will end. The other 20% of the time, the other four will have to wrestle/cage the Edoloth until he comes out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:50:14-08:00","id":823500,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea is that you pick a trigger (i.e. &quot;Moon&quot; or &quot;Blood&quot;) and its severity is determined by your Harmony. At 10 and 0 you use the Passive version, at 9, 8, 1, and 2 you use the Common version, at 7, 6, 4, and 3 you use the Specific version, and at 5 you ignore your personal Trigger. General Triggers always apply, regardless of Harmony.<br /> <br /> A common house rule is to select one Common, one Passive, and one Specific Trigger from any category instead of taking all three from the same category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:56:52-08:00","id":823507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823442-after-a-first-reading-are-passive-kuruth-triggers-too-intense?p=823496#post823496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's not impossible to control. 80% of the time, the pack's Edoloth will be like &quot;stahp it&quot; and the Kuruth will end. The other 20% of the time, the other four will have to wrestle/cage the Edoloth until he comes out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>80% seems a little high. If your pack has an Elodoth, and he hasn't used his ability yet in the chapter, and there isn't a better tactical use for it at the time, and he's far enough away from you not to be pulled into Death Rage himself, then he might pull you out. Seems pretty conditional for an 80%. And no, the rest of the pack can't just wrestle and cage you the other 20% of the time, because if they get that close to you they'll fall into Death Rage too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:00:29-08:00","id":823512,"title":"","content":"Right, forgot it was once per chapter and not once per scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:36:35-08:00","id":823617,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Thank you guys for the input. What a super helpful forum!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","name":"Avalon Polo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T03:07:24-08:00","id":824143,"title":"","content":"Last I heard you can only get hit with a personal Kuruth trigger once per night. So at low PU you'll rage for ten or 20 minutes and then be fine for the rest of the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:04:42-08:00","id":824186,"title":"","content":"Just drive Billy to some isolated spot outside of town before the moon pops up and watch from a safe distance in case some fool campers stumble upon him.<br /> <br /> Or drop him off on one of the small islets off the coast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:21:05-08:00","id":824194,"title":"","content":"These are all good points. I hope that The Pack explores these themes in more detail. Considering that the core rule book covered locations such as Basra, Detroit, and Tokyo, it would be interesting to see how urban wolves keep themselves from flying off the handle considering the numbers of potential triggers the are surrounded by.<br /> <br /> I loved Blood of the Wolf for the first edition of forsaken because it went into more depth with werewolf themes. I hope the pack does as good a job, if not better, for the second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:22:55-08:00","id":824196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823442-after-a-first-reading-are-passive-kuruth-triggers-too-intense?p=824143#post824143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I heard you can only get hit with a personal Kuruth trigger once per night. So at low PU you'll rage for ten or 20 minutes and then be fine for the rest of the night.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are in a large city, ten to twenty minutes can be a VERY long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:42:39-08:00","id":824212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/823442-after-a-first-reading-are-passive-kuruth-triggers-too-intense?p=824196#post824196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are in a large city, ten to twenty minutes can be a VERY long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah it absolutely happens. The Moon isn't everyone's trigger but death rage in public or inconvenient places is an unfortunate possibility for every werewolf. You do seem able to tell if your Harmony's out of whack, and if it's on the low end you can at least slip into the Hisil.<br /> <br /> But unwanted death rage has probably happened to every werewolf a few times in their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:54:22-08:00","id":824219,"title":"","content":"Or you take lessons from <b>Being Human</b> and you locked up yourself on nights of Auspice...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kSnF_pp70hM\" data-code=\"kSnF_pp70hM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/kSnF_pp70hM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:11:06-08:00","id":824410,"title":"","content":"Simply, the best way to deal with an Uratha in Kuruth is with Knotted Paths. Even at Primal Urge 10, he still gets lost for an additional 12 hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:04:29-08:00","id":824680,"title":"","content":"Mind you, that may be the point. Forsaken 2nd edition makes the &quot;beast within&quot; a much more powerful adversary. Part of the fear is the possibility of losing control at the worst possible moment. Maybe the challenge is maintaining the tightrope balance of harmony and not succumbing to the destructive spiral of dark ur<br /> ges. Once you start giving into Kuruth, balance becomes more difficult and degeneration begins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T02:38:48-08:00","id":828098,"title":"","content":"As others have noted, <i>Kuruth </i>can be a deadly foe, wresting control away from a werewolf in slavering jaws. Worse still, it can cascade into an entire pack going berserk. So there are a few good ways to be prepared for it:<br /> <br /> 1) Balance your Harmony. It's the best way to help prevent frequent and/or long-lasting episodes of <i>Kuruth</i>.<br /> 2) Wisdom Facet of the Inspiration Gift: Still Small Voice. It can take characters from <i>Wasu-Im </i>to a calm state.<br /> 2a) You can also use the Pack Awareness (Wisdom) Facet of the Gift of Pack. It lets the character who has it sense each of her packmates and general state and well-being (or lack thereof) up to Wisdom Renown in miles. You can also spend 1 Essence to speak telepathically with any packmate you can see, in order to use Still Small Voice from a greater distance, perhaps.<br /> 3) A werewolf skilled in Expression or possessing the Inspiring Merit, or both. She can grant your character the Inspired Condition, perhaps singing or speaking about the need for Harmony. When you go into <i>Wasu-</i><i>Im</i>, if you roll Resolve + Composure to fight for clarity for a few turns, if you roll 3 successes, you can resolve the Condition to gain an exceptional success and end the Death Rage before it starts.<br /> <br /> Various other situational means can help corral the <i>Kuruth</i>, like the suggestion of Knotted Paths above. Fetishes, unique totem powers, or the like might also help a werewolf keep a leash on her Rage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T04:52:54-08:00","id":828138,"title":"","content":"Optimizing towards Resolve + Composure can also keep the death rage at bay. The cheapest way of doing this is likely Pack Dynamics 3, which will grant you a +3 to said tests as long as you make sure to not do any lone wolf antics or your packmates don't go missing. This isn't as good as getting the Inspired condition, but it compounds its effects: An inspired, high resolve (9+ dice) werewolf can actually run around at Harmony 9/1 pretty reliably without falling into the hard rage.<br /> <br /> Chain Rage is also a good rite for controlling the rage, although not too useful at the the 8+, 2- ends of Harmony since the wolf will not have enough time to have it take effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","user":"Captain Shoe","date":". 02-11-2016, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}